@@ -190,3 +190,21 @@ content right-aligned, matching how the rest of the app aligns numeric columns.
 - **WHEN** a result's `HTTP` or `Duration` cell is colored for its response status
 - **THEN** the cell is both colored and right-aligned
 
+### Requirement: Results grid header labels share one style
+
+On the run Extraction Result grid and the run comparison Execution Results grid, every header label
+(column and group labels alike) SHALL render at the same size and weight, in the label's own letter
+case, with no added letter spacing. A label over a numeric or score column SHALL sit at the right edge
+of its column, even when some or all of its cells show only a dash; every other label SHALL sit at the
+left. Group header rows SHALL be as tall as the column header row, so the header rows are evenly spaced.
+
+#### Scenario: Default and custom headers look the same
+
+- **WHEN** the grid shows `Test Case name`, `HTTP`, `Duration`, a metric's `score` and the `Execution` group
+- **THEN** each label renders in the same typography, none of them uppercased
+
+#### Scenario: Score column with missing values stays right-aligned
+
+- **WHEN** a metric's value is missing on the first row, or on every row
+- **THEN** the metric's column label still sits at the right edge of its column
+
